1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,560
Scientists built a factory

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,160
that turns living cockroaches

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:04,280
into robots.

4
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:04,995
And it only takes

5
00:00:05,035 --> 00:00:06,430
68 seconds.

6
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:07,510
A robotic arm grabs

7
00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:08,430
a tiny computer

8
00:00:08,470 --> 00:00:09,190
and attaches it

9
00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:10,570
to the cockroach’s back.

10
00:00:10,610 --> 00:00:12,245
Then tiny electrodes deliver

11
00:00:12,285 --> 00:00:13,365
electrical pulses

12
00:00:13,405 --> 00:00:14,890
that can make the bug turn.

13
00:00:14,930 --> 00:00:15,930
So now, instead of

14
00:00:15,970 --> 00:00:18,000
building tiny robots from scratch…

15
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:18,920
Scientists can use

16
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:20,600
actual living insects.

17
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:22,270
And here’s the crazy part.

18
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:23,065
They’ve already sent

19
00:00:23,105 --> 00:00:24,265
cyborg cockroaches

20
00:00:24,305 --> 00:00:25,585
into a real earthquake

21
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:26,740
disaster zone.

22
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:27,655
Which means we’re not

23
00:00:27,695 --> 00:00:29,015
just building robots anymore.

24
00:00:29,055 --> 00:00:31,150
We’re turning bugs into them.

